    "result_text": "Full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec requires a `displayName` formatted as `'LastName, FirstName'` on the owner response. Since the acceptance test reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, the value must be produced wherever an `Owner` is serialized \u2014 so I put it at the single central mapping point rather than in a per-endpoint responder function.\n\nTwo small changes, no function bodies grown:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")` annotation to the existing `toOwnerDto` abstract method.\n\nThis keeps structural impact minimal: I avoided adding a method to the large `Owner` model class (high WMC_other) and avoided touching any of the endpoint pipeline function classes. MapStruct emits the concatenation directly in generated code, so no new function bodies were introduced. `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesDisplayName` and the full suite pass.",
